  "query_preview": "..High pressure aloft was centered over north Texas\nwith a strong trough centered over the Pacific Northwest early \nMonday morning.\n\nFor today...A shortwave disturbance moving through the Pacific\nNorthwest trough will brush Arizona then move to the northeast \nthrough the day. The net effect of this feature will be to deliver\na drier air mass to most of northern Arizona. The only areas that\nwill avoid this drying will be the eastern Mogollon Rim, White \nMountains and to some degree the Chuska Mountains. Most areas \nwill see partly to mostly cloud skies as mid to upper level \nmoisture streams across the area but low chances for any\nprecipitation. Substantial low-level moisture will be confined to\nthe eastern portions of the forecast area.\n\nFrom Tuesday into Thursday...High pressure will gradually build\nback over Arizona from the east. Monsoon moisture will continue \nto linger and even gradually increase through this period. As a \nresult, the shower and thunderstorm threat will continue across \nthe high terrain of eastern Arizona but gradually spread westward \nalong the Mogollon Rim. Any heavy rain potential is expected to \nremain confined to the White Mountains region. Activity will \ncontinue to be focused in the afternoon and evening. Look for \nwarmer temperatures as the high builds over northern Arizona with \nmountain temperatures climbing to the upper 70s to mid 80s and 95\nto 105 at lower elevations.\n\nLooking at Friday onward...Additional troughing enters the western\nstates pushing the high center to the east. It isn't clear that\nthis next trough will sweep monsoon moisture away. In fact, most\nmodels suggest monsoon moisture will interact with disturbances\nmoving through the western trough modulated to some degree by\ndaytime heating. We will have to wait and see on this one because\nif the trough comes in stronger than models currently show drying\nwill likely follow. On the other hand, if trough energy remains on\nthe northern periphery of the low-level monsoon moisture it could\nremain unsettled, most likely day and night.",
